      "scope": "Actual8086 DOS startup diagnostic uses BIOS/canonical row owners, shared-view normalized-key adapter, and actual PROGRAM/COMSPEC/EXEC with BIOS return keys. PROGRAM reacquires the UART inside the diagnostic; the normal main loop is not entered and the peer sends no data. Geometry/video/shadow, exclusive output refusal, unchanged synthetic PRM/image, zero serial output,42-byte UART/PIC/vector restoration and diagnostic package rejection are checked. Larger-profile/ASPECT composition, live BBS/SIP/analog and physical acceptance remain separate. Additionally sixteen actual DOS source-built XLTEDIT/EXEC/save/confirmation round trips at25/28/43/50 physical rows with visible status and an explicit synthetic table change byte0 to88 then0. Full before/after frames, canonical/physical height, child exit, selected256-byte active table, final disk identity and absence of recovery remnants are checked. Parent UART ownership is restored but peer sends no data; post-return RX/TX is covered separately by the boundary-modeled CPU checker."
